    "content": "The 2026 Women's Selection Sunday took place on March 15, 2026, setting the 68-team NCAA Tournament field with the UConn Huskies earning the No. 1 overall seed after an undefeated regular season. UConn headlines the Fort Worth 1 region, while top-tier seeds include Texas, South Carolina, and UCLA. The tournament begins with the First Four on March 18-19. Key 2026 Selection Sunday & Tournament Details Selection Show: Sunday, March 15, 8 p.m. ET on ESPN. Top Seeds (Regional #1 Seeds): UConn, Texas, UCLA, South Carolina. First Four: March 18–19. First Round: March 20–21. Second Round: March 22–23. Regional Rounds (Sweet 16/Elite Eight): March 27–30 in Fort Worth, Texas, and Sacramento, California. Final Four: April 3 & 5, at the Mortgage Matchup Center in Phoenix, Arizona. Top Seed Highlights UConn Huskies: Named No. 1 overall seed (11th time in program history) with a 50-game win streak. They face UTSA in the first round. Texas Longhorns: Secured a No. 1 seed (31-3). South Carolina & UCLA: Also secured top spots in the bracket. Tournament Context The top 16 teams were announced prior to the full reveal. This is the first tournament utilizing the 2026-2031 future site structure, with the Final Four in Phoenix, NCAA.com reports.",
